13
00:00:30,974 --> 00:00:33,053
Chemists call how much of the nitrogen and

14
00:00:33,134 --> 00:00:36,973
hydrogen has become ammonia,
once settled, the equilibrium

15
00:00:37,054 --> 00:00:38,013
yield.

16
00:00:38,094 --> 00:00:40,813
For one starting gas
and pressure, more ammonia

17
00:00:40,894 --> 00:00:43,853
in the settled gas means a higher yield.

18
00:00:43,934 --> 00:00:47,373
The forward reaction gives
out heat, 92 kilojoules

19
00:00:47,454 --> 00:00:50,013
for each mole of nitrogen, so heat goes

20
00:00:50,094 --> 00:00:51,293
