37
00:01:32,434 --> 00:01:35,153
Here are three temperatures
at the same pressure,

38
00:01:35,234 --> 00:01:38,273
200 atmospheres,
with the gas starting as three

39
00:01:38,354 --> 00:01:40,513
hydrogen to one nitrogen.

40
00:01:40,594 --> 00:01:42,433
These numbers are illustrative.

41
00:01:42,514 --> 00:01:44,473
The cool one would settle at about sixty

42
00:01:44,514 --> 00:01:47,473
percent ammonia, but it crawls, so the gas

43
00:01:47,554 --> 00:01:49,393
leaves with only a little.

44
00:01:49,474 --> 00:01:51,473
The hot one settles at once, at only

45
00:01:51,634 --> 00:01:52,913
about nine.

46
00:01:52,994 --> 00:01:55,553
The middle one would settle
at about twenty-five,

47
00:01:55,594 --> 00:01:57,633
and it gets close in the time available,

48
00:01:57,754 --> 00:01:58,993
so it gives the most.

49
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:01,880
So what does the iron do?

50
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:05,400
It gives the molecules
a lower-energy pathway in

51
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:08,520
both directions, so the
middle temperature is fast

52
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:09,000
